# patterns.local.conf — CONSUMER-LOCAL damage-control additions (TEMPLATE)
# =============================================================================
# Copy this file to `patterns.local.conf` (drop the `.example`) in this same
# directory to add repo-local guards to damage-control.sh WITHOUT editing
# damage-control.sh or patterns.yaml — both of which the claude-pattern sync
# OVERWRITES on every run. `patterns.local.conf` is a SIDECAR the source never
# ships, so no sync overwrites or deletes it (and a default `*.local.*` exclude +
# a retired-path guard back that up). See
# docs/operations/skill-upgrade-propagation.md.
#
# GRAMMAR — one `key: value` per line. Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored.
# This is NOT YAML (deliberately named `.conf`, not `.yaml`, so you don't mirror
# patterns.yaml's nested shape). Recognized keys:
#
#   block:      <ERE>   a Bash-command regex to BLOCK   (grep -E, case-sensitive)
#   blockCI:    <ERE>   a Bash-command regex to BLOCK   (case-insensitive)
#   ask:        <ERE>   a Bash-command regex to ASK before running
#   askCI:      <ERE>   a Bash-command regex to ASK     (case-insensitive)
#   zeroAccess: <glob>  a file-path fragment/glob to BLOCK for read/write/delete
#   readOnly:   <glob>  a file-path fragment/glob to block for write/edit/delete
#   noDelete:   <glob>  a file-path fragment/glob to block for delete only
#
# SEMANTICS:
#   • Additions can only ESCALATE. A local `block:` is evaluated BEFORE the
#     built-in safe-rm allow and the built-in ask loops, so it wins over a
#     built-in allow/ask. A local rule can never weaken a built-in guard.
#   • Values are matched as DATA — never sourced or eval'd. `$(...)`, backticks,
#     and `;` are matched literally, not executed.
#   • Fail-open to the BUILT-INS: if this file is missing/unreadable/garbage, the
#     built-in guards still enforce.
#   • A malformed line, unknown key, invalid regex, unreadable file, or CRLF is
#     reported to stderr AND to ~/.claude/logs/security.jsonl (never silently
#     dropped) — check there if a rule seems inert.
#
# CAUTIONS:
#   • These are regexes fed to `grep -E`. A catastrophic-backtracking pattern can
#     hang the hook; keep patterns simple.
#   • A broad rule like `block: .*` denies EVERY command (self-DoS). The failure
#     direction is over-block, never under-block — but test your rules.
#
# Kill switch: DAMAGE_CONTROL_DISABLE_LOCAL=1   Override path: DAMAGE_CONTROL_LOCAL_FILE
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WORKED EXAMPLE — the "MOBILE STORE ONE-WAY DOORS" guard (the real cleanscale/
# cleanrev block that the sync twice wiped, now expressible as a sidecar):
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# block:   eas submit
# block:   eas build.*--auto-submit
# block:   --auto-submit
# block:   asc-submit-build\.mjs
# block:   androidpublisher
# block:   fastlane (deliver|supply)
# ask:     eas build

# (Delete the examples below or replace with your own before use.)
